Subject: Re: Urgent AC-2025-LON-004293 Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Jus=
tice and Others/ RE: AC-2025-LON-004293 =E2=80=93 Clarifications Requested (Urgent=
 N463 Application)
Importance: High

=20

Dear Ms Ramchurn,

Thank you for your email. For the avoidance of all doubt, and to assist the=
 Court in progressing the N463 without further delay, I provide the followin=
g firm clarification.

=20

1. No ongoing Family or Financial Remedy proceedings / No judicial challeng=
e

As confirmed on 2 December 2025 at 8:38 am, all Family Court and Financial =
Remedy proceedings between myself and Mr Zahmoul are fully concluded. There =
are no live hearings, no listed reviews, no reserved judgments, and no remai=
ning applications at any level of the Family Court or High Court Family Divi=
sion.

For absolute clarity, my judicial review does not challenge any judicial ac=
t, decision, finding or order. The claim is directed solely at the administr=
ative acts and omissions of HMCTS and the Secretary of State for Justice. No=
thing in my claim invites the Administrative Court to revisit, reconsider or=
 question any judicial decision.

=20

Every ground in my JR concerns administrative functions and statutory dutie=
s for which HMCTS and the Secretary of State for Justice are accountable, in=
cluding=E2=80=94

=E2=80=A2 the administrative handling, storage and escalation of evidence and inf=
ormation I provided;

=E2=80=A2 the administrative management of disability information and participati=
on measures;

=E2=80=A2 reasonable adjustment duties under ss.20=E2=80=9321 Equality Act 2010;

=E2=80=A2 the Public Sector Equality Duty under s.149;

=E2=80=A2 safeguarding and communication obligations;

=E2=80=A2 administrative compliance with the Autism Act 2009 statutory guidance a=
nd related public law duties.

=20

Any reference to =E2=80=9Ccriminal evidence=E2=80=9D in my papers concerns only the adm=
inistrative handling of that material by HMCTS. It does not relate to any ju=
dicial assessment or judicial function. The claim therefore falls squarely w=
ithin the Administrative Court=E2=80=99s jurisdiction.

=20

2. Identification of Defendants

The Secretary of State for Justice (First Defendant) is the correct legal p=
ersonification of the Ministry of Justice. I did not intend to add the Minis=
try of Justice as a separate Third Defendant. Where =E2=80=9CMoJ=E2=80=9D appears, it is=
 shorthand for the First Defendant.

=20

Accordingly, the Defendants remain as listed in Section 1 of the claim form=
:
Secretary of State for Justice
HM Courts & Tribunals Service
=20

Service has already been completed on both.

=20

3. Statutory duties and urgency

In light of the above, I respectfully remind the Court that the handling of=
 my N463 and the underlying administrative issues engages fully active statu=
tory duties, including:

=E2=80=A2 Equality Act 2010 ss.20=E2=80=9321 (continuing and anticipatory duty to make =
reasonable adjustments),

=E2=80=A2 Equality Act 2010 s.29 (non-discriminatory service provision),

=E2=80=A2 the Public Sector Equality Duty (s.149),

=E2=80=A2 the overriding objective concerning vulnerable litigants, and

=E2=80=A2 HMCTS=E2=80=99s own duties of safeguarding, communication, accessibility and =
procedural fairness.

=20

Given my deteriorating medical position and the subject matter of the claim=
=E2=80=94which directly concerns earlier failures to implement these duties=E2=80=94I mu=
st emphasise that any further delay risks replicating and compounding the ve=
ry breaches raised in the JR. The Court is now under a present and ongoing o=
bligation to ensure that this urgent application is handled in a manner comp=
liant with these statutory duties. I am therefore grateful for confirmation =
that the N463 will now proceed promptly to judicial consideration and to a p=
ublic, oral hearing.

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

AC-2025-LON-004293

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

=20

On 03/12/2025, 2:42=E2=80=AFAM, "Administrative Court Office, Case Progression" <=
administrativecourtoffice.caseprogression@justice.gov.uk> wrote:

=20

=20

Dear Ms Zahmoul,

=20

We acknowledge receipt of your applications. We understand that you are see=
king for permission to apply for judicial review challenging the acts or omi=
ssions of the Defendants in handling criminal evidence you have provided reg=
arding Mr Zahmoul.=20

=20

Any urgent application will have to go before a judge for consideration on =
whether to list it as an oral hearing or a rolled-up hearing. Therefore, you=
r request for an oral hearing to deal with the urgent application will be pu=
t to the judge for consideration with all the necessary information.=20

=20

To assist the Administrative Court to understand the current position to de=
al with it expeditiously in respect of your application for urgent considera=
tion, please can you confirm if there are there are any ongoing financial re=
medy case or active Family case at the moment?  If so at what level of court=
 and what stage the proceedings are at.=20

=20

Please could you also clarify the following regarding your claim form:

Under Section 1 of your claim form, you have listed only the Secretary of S=
tate for Justice (First Defendant) and HMCTS (Second Defendant). However, in=
 other parts of your papers, you have mentioned the Ministry of Justice (MOJ=
).

Could you confirm whether you intended for the MOJ to be included as a Thir=
d Defendant under Section 1 of your claim form? If so, they will also need t=
o be served with the sealed claim form and bundle.

=20

=20

We will be grateful if you can provide us a respond shortly.

=20

Kind Regards

Meera Ramchurn

Administrative Court Office |Case Progression Officer | King's Bench Divisi=
on | HMCTS | Royal Courts of Justice| Strand, London | WC2A 2LL | Phone: 020=
 7947 6000 | Web: www.gov.uk/hmcts

If replying by email, please use the following address: administrativecourt=
office.caseprogression@justice.gov.uk

